  "value": "image is a non-empty string over \"0\" and \"1\". One operation removes any single character and appends it to the end of the string. Return the minimum number of operations that turn image into its reverse. Characters never moved keep their relative order at the front, so the answer is the length minus the longest prefix of the reverse that is a subsequence of image.",
